# Backend

Django + Django REST Framework service for `{{projectName}}`.

## App structure

```
backend/
├── manage.py           # Django CLI entry point
├── config/             # project package
│   ├── settings/
│   │   ├── base.py     # shared settings (apps, DRF, storage, logging)
│   │   ├── local.py    # development — DEBUG, dev SECRET_KEY fallback
│   │   └── production.py  # deployed — everything from the environment
│   ├── urls.py         # root URLconf — mounts every app under api/
{{#if withCelery}}
│   ├── celery.py       # Celery application (worker/beat entry point)
{{/if}}
│   ├── wsgi.py         # gunicorn entry point
│   └── asgi.py
└── apps/               # one Django app per domain
    ├── core/           # health endpoint, shared plumbing
    ├── users/          # custom User model (AUTH_USER_MODEL) + read-only API
{{#if withS3}}
    ├── files/          # file uploads stored on S3 / MinIO
{{/if}}
    └── <your-app>/     # models.py, serializers.py, services.py, views.py,
                        # urls.py, admin.py, migrations/, tests/
```

Conventions enforced by `dude lint` (see `.claude/rules/BE/` at the project
root): explicit serializer `fields`, explicit `permission_classes` on every
view, ORM **writes only in `services.py`**, every app has migrations and a
`tests/` package, models define `__str__` + `Meta.ordering`.

## Requirements

- Python 3.13+
- [uv](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/) (recommended)
- Docker (recommended for full-stack dev)
{{#if withPostgres}}
- PostgreSQL 17 (SQLite is used when `DATABASE_URL` is unset)
{{/if}}
{{#if withCelery}}
- Redis 7
{{/if}}

## Run with Docker

```bash
docker compose up --build
```

Migrations run automatically on container start via `start.sh`.

After changing a model:

```bash
dude db makemigration --message "describe change"
dude db migrate
```

Create an admin account for <http://localhost:8000/admin/>:

```bash
dude db superuser
```
{{#if withCelery}}

Celery worker{{#if withCeleryBeat}}, beat scheduler{{/if}} and Flower monitor are started automatically by docker compose.
Flower UI: <http://localhost:5555>
{{/if}}

## Run locally (without Docker)

```bash
uv sync
uv run python manage.py migrate
uv run python manage.py runserver 0.0.0.0:8000
```

Then open <http://localhost:8000/api/health/> — the interactive API reference
lives at <http://localhost:8000/api/docs/> (Scalar, rendered from
`backend/templates/api-docs.html`) and the raw OpenAPI schema at
<http://localhost:8000/api/schema/>.

The reference's prose — authentication, conventions, the domain lifecycle — is
hand-written in `backend/config/api_docs.py`. Keep it current: the schema is
generated, that file is not.

## Tests

```bash
uv run pytest            # or `dude test --backend` from the project root
```
